  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two integers NNN and XXX.\n\nCount the number of distinct arrays of length **at most** NNN, whose LCM is equal to XXX.\n\nThat is, find the number of arrays AAA such that:\n\n\n1≤∣A∣≤N1 \\leq |A| \\leq N1≤∣A∣≤N, where ∣A∣|A|∣A∣ denotes the length of AAA; and\nlcm(A1,A2,A3,…,A∣A∣)=X\\text{lcm}(A_1, A_2, A_3, \\ldots, A_{|A|}) = Xlcm(A1​,A2​,A3​,…,A∣A∣​)=X\nTwo arrays AAA and BBB are considered different if:\n\n\nAAA and BBB have different lengths; or\nAAA and BBB have the same length, but Ai≠BiA_i \\neq B_iAi​=Bi​ for some index 1≤i≤∣A∣1 \\leq i \\leq |A|1≤i≤∣A∣.\nThe answer may be large, so compute it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line containing two space-separated integers NNN and XXX, the parameters specified in the statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of possible arrays with length at most NNN and LCM equal to XXX, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤X≤1091 \\leq X \\leq 10^91≤X≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 3\n10000 6\n156324 959345256",
        "output": "4\n682692428\n568466415",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: We're looking for arrays of length at most 222 and whose LCM is 333.\nThe only such arrays are [3],[1,3],[3,1],[3,3][3], [1, 3], [3, 1], [3, 3][3],[1,3],[3,1],[3,3]."
      }
    ]
